  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PRAIRIES: PROTECTING WETLANDS AND UPLAND</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will enable long-term securement and management of prime waterfowl breeding habitat within the Prairie and Aspen Parkland ecoregions of Alberta, Saskatchewan, and Manitoba. Project activities include fee simple acquisition of 710 acres, 240 acres of conservation easements, and management activities on 77,929 acres. Project accomplishments will benefit many species of waterfowl, as well as colonial waterbirds, wading birds and grassland birds</narrative>
  </description>
